## Why This Is Asked
This question tests deep production debugging skills, including multi-tenant cache management, Redis eviction policies, and safe rollout procedures under traffic.

## Key Concepts
- Redis eviction policies (volatile-lru, allkeys-lru, etc.) and TTL management
- Multi-tenant namespace isolation in Redis using key prefixes
- Canary rollout strategies (e.g., Argo Rollouts or manual phased deployments)
- Observability: Redis INFO metrics, hit/miss ratios, and application latency metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify current eviction policy
const evictionPolicy = await redis.configGet('maxmemory-policy');
console.log('Current eviction policy:', evictionPolicy);

// Check keyspace stats
const info = await redis.info('stats');
const hits = info.match(/keyspace_hits:(\d+)/)[1];
const misses = info.match(/keyspace_misses:(\d+)/)[1];
const hitRate = hits / (hits + misses);
console.log('Hit rate:', hitRate);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of per-tenant feature flags and zero-downtime rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes ConfigMaps and pod configuration propagation
- Environment variables vs mounted files for configuration delivery
- Canary deployments and rollback safety mechanisms
- Observability practices and latency budget management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Reads a per-tenant flag from environment variable with fallback to false
function isBetaEnabled(tenantId){
  const cfg = JSON.parse(process.env.TENANT_FLAGS || '{}');
  return !!cfg[tenantId]?.betaRoute;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical diagnostic thinking for a real-time multi-tenant pipeline using Redis streams and Kubernetes rollouts, emphasizing per-tenant lag visibility, safe canary rollout, and rollback procedures.

## Key Concepts

- Redis Streams per-tenant counters and consumer group lag monitoring
- Kubernetes deployment rollouts and canary deployment patterns
- XINFO, XRANGE, XPENDING commands for stream health diagnostics
- Latency targets and per-tenant QoS validation during rollouts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js pseudo-consumer outline for per-tenant Redis stream processing
const redis = require('redis');
const client = redis.createClient({ host: REDIS_HOST, port: REDIS_PORT });

async function processTenantEvents(tenantId) {
  const streamKey = `analytics:tenant:${tenantId}`;
  const groupName = 'analytics-group';

  try {
    // Read pending messages for this tenant
    const pending = await client.xPending(streamKey, groupName);
    if (pending > 0) {
      console.log(`Tenant ${tenantId} has ${pending} pending events`);
    }

    // Process new events
    const messages = await client.xReadGroup(groupName, 'consumer-1', 
      [{ key: streamKey, id: '>' }], { COUNT: 10, BLOCK: 1000 });

    for (const message of messages) {
      await processEvent(message);
      await client.xAck(streamKey, groupName, message.id);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error processing tenant ${tenantId}:`, error);
  }
}
```
